  "scenario": "A commercial greenhouse tomato operation growing vine tomatoes has seen marketable yield fall about 30% over two growing cycles, and the shortfall has repeated across successive plantings. The decline set in after a switch to a new irrigation-water source following a well upgrade. The agronomists' leading theories are under-watering or a nitrogen shortfall, so they are considering more water and feed. New leaves have looked paler than usual between the veins. Routine soil and tissue panels read broadly within range. The irrigation, fertigation, and amendment dosing are all adjustable, and dosing and amendment equipment is available. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available controls or amendments, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the loss and what to do about it.",
